      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تناكحوا</span></b>  <i>They intermarried; contracted
marriages together.</i> (Commencing a trad. in
the Jámi' es-Sagheer.) [And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَاكَحَا</span> <i>Se invicem
futuerunt:</i> see 6, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ردف</span>] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَاكَحَتِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَشْجَارُ</span> <i>The trees became drawn,</i> or <i>connected,
together.</i> (Msb.)

